# A deposition velocity in place of the bottom-level sink, and below-cloud wet
# scavenging. DUST-3 items 2 and 3; DUST-7.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. ExoPlaSim's aerosol has exactly one removal path,
# sedimentation, plus a line at the bottom of the tracer loop that removes 99% of
# the bottom layer every timestep. `aeolian/notes/in-model-dust.md` measured what
# that line implies against this world's own bottom layer and it is two orders of
# magnitude faster than any measured dust deposition velocity, and it does not
# scale with the timestep, so the implied velocity is inversely proportional to
# the step. A rate that depends on the integration step is not a rate. It has to
# go before any emission is calibrated, because it multiplies whatever is
# injected by 0.01 every step.
#
# There is also no wet deposition of any kind: `aerocore`'s argument list
# contains no precipitation field. That is DUST-7, and `aeolian/README.md` says
# of this project's own offline chain that without the wet term the fine mode's
# lifetime is out by an order of magnitude, so it is a first-order sink rather
# than a refinement. Worth recording that the LMD Generic PCM has no wet
# deposition for its aerosols either: this is a common omission in exoplanet
# GCMs, not a peculiarity of ExoPlaSim.
#
# BOTH TERMS DEFAULT TO OFF, and that is `WORKFLOW.md` A3 rather than taste. Both
# arms of an A/B have to come from ONE executable and differ only by a namelist
# key, because the low-I/O patch changes the restart layout and arms built either
# side of a rebuild cannot share a restart at all. With `ldepvel = 0` and
# `lwetdep = 0` this patch reproduces the unpatched model exactly: the legacy
# sink line is unchanged, no precipitation is gathered, and no extra collective
# call is made.
#
# BASE. ExoPlaSim 3.4.2 plus exoplasim-3.4.2-aerocore-defects.patch, which has to
# be applied first. That base is
#
#   aerocore.f90  b2d12c47a82097515e3e09f55d0994b934a647a05807ffc21e23a5f9a7c54877
#   aeromod.f90   1b666c49b8e2c3dabdb8074d9d060d939c7506073215afda490086c5af6caf3e
#
# It does NOT depend on the defect patch for the code it edits, but it does
# depend on it for the physics to make sense: until the bottom level stops being
# updated twice, the sedimentation flux out of the atmosphere cancels itself and
# no deposition velocity can be measured against anything.
#
# RESIDENT-DESTINED, NOT YET RESIDENT. Listed in `PENDING_PATCHES` in
# `exoplasim/scripts/rebuild_binaries.py`; it moves to `RESIDENT_PATCHES` in the
# commit that applies it and rebuilds every binary.
#
# WHAT IT ADDS.
#
#  1. Five `aero_nl` keys: `ldepvel`, `vdaero`, `lwetdep`, `scava`, `scavb`.
#     `aero_nl` is read in `aero_ini`, which runs on NROOT only and only when
#     `nsela > 0 .and. l_aero > 0`; `aerocore` also runs on NROOT only, so none
#     of these needs a broadcast. Note that `radmod.f90` DECLARES a second
#     `aero_nl` group and never reads it, so the two lists have diverged; that
#     declaration is dead and is left alone because `radmod.f90` is not this
#     patch's business.
#
#  2. `ldepvel = 1`: the bottom layer keeps `exp(-vdaero*dt/dz)` per step, with
#     `dz` built from that layer's own pressure thickness and gas density. The
#     rate is then a property of the atmosphere rather than of the step, which is
#     a test that can fail: halve `deltsec` and the removal per unit time must not
#     move. The legacy line fails it by construction.
#
#     `vdaero` is the NON-gravitational part of dry deposition, turbulent
#     transfer and impaction. Sedimentation to the surface is already the
#     `gz(nl)` term in the final update, so a Stokes velocity here would deposit
#     the same mass twice. The right long-run form is a resistance model,
#     `1/(r_a + r_b)`, which needs the friction velocity and the roughness; those
#     are not gathered today and the emission scheme (item 4 of the design note)
#     has to gather them anyway. Until then this is a declared constant and it is
#     declared in `aeolian/config/dust.yaml`, not here.
#
#  3. `lwetdep = 1`: below-cloud scavenging at `Lambda = scava * p**scavb` with
#     `p` the total precipitation rate in mm/h, from `dprl + dprc` in m/s. That
#     is Sportisse (2007) and it is the same form and the same coefficients the
#     offline chain uses, so the two chains can be compared rather than merely
#     contrasted. Applied through the whole column rather than below a diagnosed
#     cloud base, which is the offline chain's own approximation and is kept
#     deliberately for the same reason.
#
#  4. NO DEFAULTS for `vdaero`, `scava` and `scavb`. `aero_ini` ABORTS when a
#     switch is on and its coefficient is not set, in the same way `radini`
#     aborts on `ndustrad = 1` with `dustqlw` at zero. A plausible-looking
#     default in Fortran would be a fourth place for a number that
#     `aeolian/config/dust.yaml` already owns, and it would go stale silently.
#
# WHAT IT DELIBERATELY IS NOT. No emission scheme and no boundary fields: the
# source term is still `fcoeff*land`. No size bins. Nothing in `radmod.f90`.
#
